#. type: multicols
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:310
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\subsection*{\\pagetarget{Schools of Magic}{Schools of Magic}}\n"
"All Spell cards belong to one School of Magic\\index{Schools of Magic}: either Air, Fire, Earth or Water.\n"
"Spells with one School symbol on them are called \\textbf{Basic Spells}\\index{Basic Spell}, while Spells with four identical symbols are called \\textbf{Expert Spells}\\index{Expert Spell}.\n"
"\\textbf{\\wikilink{spells/magic_arrow}{Magic Arrow}} is a Basic Spell; when casting the \\textbf{Magic Arrow}, you must select which School it belongs to.\n"
"By default there's no difference, but certain game effects can refer to specific Schools and to Basic/Expert Spells.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\\subsection*{\\pagetarget{Schools of Magic}{Écoles de magie}}\n"
"Toutes les cartes Sort appartiennent à une école de magie\\index{Schools of Magic} : Air, Feu, Terre ou Eau.\n"
"Les sorts portant un symbole d’école sont des \\textbf{sorts Basiques}\\index{Basic Spell}, ceux qui en portent quatre identiques sont des \\textbf{sorts Experts}\\index{Expert Spell}.\n"
"La \\textbf{\\wikilink{spells/magic_arrow}{Flèche magique}} est un sort Basique ; en la lançant, vous devez choisir son école.\n"
"Par défaut, cela ne change rien, mais certains effets de jeu mentionnent des écoles précises et les sorts Basiques/Experts.\n"
"\n"

